    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0390" n="366" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg366"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Morris.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 75.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 28, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch No. 81, of the 3d instant,
                    has been received. Your proceedings relative to the presentation of the pistols
                    to his highness Kibrisili Pasha, as well as your reply to the note addressed to
                    you by the Porte concerning sea postal service on the Turkish coast, are
                    approved.</p>
                <pb facs="0391" n="367" xml:id="pg367"/>
                <p>The energy and liberality displayed by the present Sultan in his administration
                    of the affairs of the empire are perceived with much satisfaction in this
                    country.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Joy Morris</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Constantinople.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
